{"ref":"BDB, עֹ֫מֶר²","hw":"עֹ֫מֶר²","html":"† II. <big><span dir=\"rtl\">עֹ֫מֶר</span></big>  <strong>n.m.</strong> <sup><a data-ref=\"Exodus 16:22\" href=\"/Exodus.16.22\">Ex 16:22</a></sup> <strong>omer (</strong>cf. Arabic <span dir=\"rtl\">غُمَرٌ</span> <em>small drinking cup</em> or <em>bowl;</em> relation to i. <span dir=\"rtl\">ע׳</span> obscure<strong>)</strong>;—a measure, only <a data-ref=\"Exodus 16\" href=\"/Exodus.16\">Ex 16</a>;—the measure itself v <a data-ref=\"Exodus 16:18\" href=\"/Exodus.16.18\">18</a>, <a data-ref=\"Exodus 16:32\" href=\"/Exodus.16.32\">32</a>, <a data-ref=\"Exodus 16:33\" href=\"/Exodus.16.33\">33</a>; amount measured v <a data-ref=\"Exodus 16:16\" href=\"/Exodus.16.16\">16</a>, <a data-ref=\"Exodus 16:22\" href=\"/Exodus.16.22\">22</a>; = 1/10 ephah v <a data-ref=\"Exodus 16:36\" href=\"/Exodus.16.36\">36</a>; 𝔊 γόμορ.","next":"BDB, עָמִיר","prev":"BDB, עֹ֫מֶר"}